doc:sch-6-sec-19-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "19(3) Decision by the Attorney-General to refuse consent to transfer" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the Attorney-General decides under subsection (1) to refuse consent to the transfer on terms proposed by the transfer country, the Attorney-General: (a) must notify the transfer country of the decision; and (b) may advise the transfer country in writing that consent may be given if the transfer country proposes a variation of those terms, including any variation suggested by the Attorney-General. Note: This section applies separately for each occasion where the transfer country proposes varied terms. This means the Attorney-General can consider whether to refuse consent under subsection (1) in relation to each variation of terms proposed by the transfer country.  Schedule 6  Refusal of consent to international transfer of prisoners  Crimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus) Act 2023 No. 63, 2023" ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-6-sec-19-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "19(4) Decision by the Attorney-General to refuse consent to transfer"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-19-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the Attorney-General decides under subsection (1) to refuse consent to the transfer on terms proposed by the transfer country, sections 20 to 23 do not apply for the transfer on those particular terms. Note: Sections 20 to 23 continue to apply for the transfer on any proposed variation of those terms, unless the Attorney-General has refused consent to the varied terms under subsection (1) of this section." ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the Attorney-General decides under subsection (1) to refuse consent to the transfer on terms proposed by the transfer country, sections 20 to 23 do not apply for the transfer on those particular terms. Note: Sections 20 to 23 continue to apply for the transfer on any proposed variation of those terms, unless the Attorney-General has refused consent to the varied terms under subsection (1) of this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a1cab01f902d0dace275f0e1b6c500d7fbf776d3d7dabf6c7e7c7fe6f28e6e5d" ;
