doc:sch-6-sec-19-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "19(4) Decision by the Attorney-General to refuse consent to transfer" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the Attorney-General decides under subsection (1) to refuse consent to the transfer on terms proposed by the transfer country, sections 20 to 23 do not apply for the transfer on those particular terms. Note: Sections 20 to 23 continue to apply for the transfer on any proposed variation of those terms, unless the Attorney-General has refused consent to the varied terms under subsection (1) of this section." ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-6-sec-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3 Subsection 20(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-3 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute: (1) If the transfer country consents to the transfer of the prisoner on terms that it proposes, the Attorney-General must: (a) give any State Ministers and Territory Ministers whose consent is required for the transfer to have appropriate Ministerial consent: (i) a copy of the application given under section 16; and (ii) any other information the Attorney-General considers relevant; and (b) notify the following of the proposed terms on which the transfer country has given consent to the transfer, including the proposed method by which the sentence of imprisonment will be enforced by the transfer country: (i) each Minister concerned; (ii) unless earlier notified under subsection 19(2) of those proposed terms—the prisoner (or the prisoner’s representative). (1A) Each Minister concerned may: (a) advise the Attorney-General of any matters that Minister considers relevant to the processing of the application; and (b) request the Attorney-General to obtain information from the transfer country that is relevant to that Minister’s assessment of the application." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute: (1) If the transfer country consents to the transfer of the prisoner on terms that it proposes, the Attorney-General must: (a) give any State Ministers and Territory Ministers whose consent is required for the transfer to have appropriate Ministerial consent: (i) a copy of the application given under section 16; and (ii) any other information the Attorney-General considers relevant; and (b) notify the following of the proposed terms on which the transfer country has given consent to the transfer, including the proposed method by which the sentence of imprisonment will be enforced by the transfer country: (i) each Minister concerned; (ii) unless earlier notified under subsection 19(2) of those proposed terms—the prisoner (or the prisoner’s representative). (1A) Each Minister concerned may: (a) advise the Attorney-General of any matters that Minister considers relevant to the processing of the application; and (b) request the Attorney-General to obtain information from the transfer country that is relevant to that Minister’s assessment of the application."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-6-sec-3-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-6-sec-3-ss-1a ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023.pdf, p.22" .
doc:sch-6-sec-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "3 Subsection 20(1)" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute: (1) If the transfer country consents to the transfer of the prisoner on terms that it proposes, the Attorney-General must: (a) give any State Ministers and Territory Ministers whose consent is required for the transfer to have appropriate Ministerial consent: (i) a copy of the application given under section 16; and (ii) any other information the Attorney-General considers relevant; and (b) notify the following of the proposed terms on which the transfer country has given consent to the transfer, including the proposed method by which the sentence of imprisonment will be enforced by the transfer country: (i) each Minister concerned; (ii) unless earlier notified under subsection 19(2) of those proposed terms—the prisoner (or the prisoner’s representative). (1A) Each Minister concerned may: (a) advise the Attorney-General of any matters that Minister considers relevant to the processing of the application; and (b) request the Attorney-General to obtain information from the transfer country that is relevant to that Minister’s assessment of the application." ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-6-sec-3-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3(1) Subsection 20(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-3-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the transfer country consents to the transfer of the prisoner on terms that it proposes, the Attorney-General must: (a) give any State Ministers and Territory Ministers whose consent is required for the transfer to have appropriate Ministerial consent: (i) a copy of the application given under section 16; and (ii) any other information the Attorney-General considers relevant; and (b) notify the following of the proposed terms on which the transfer country has given consent to the transfer, including the proposed method by which the sentence of imprisonment will be enforced by the transfer country: (i) each Minister concerned; (ii) unless earlier notified under subsection 19(2) of those proposed terms—the prisoner (or the prisoner’s representative)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the transfer country consents to the transfer of the prisoner on terms that it proposes, the Attorney-General must: (a) give any State Ministers and Territory Ministers whose consent is required for the transfer to have appropriate Ministerial consent: (i) a copy of the application given under section 16; and (ii) any other information the Attorney-General considers relevant; and (b) notify the following of the proposed terms on which the transfer country has given consent to the transfer, including the proposed method by which the sentence of imprisonment will be enforced by the transfer country: (i) each Minister concerned; (ii) unless earlier notified under subsection 19(2) of those proposed terms—the prisoner (or the prisoner’s representative)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1a8bf48eae89171cb0d580f3c56eb64ce8f75297c4c14c29b1823e96363cd459" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-act-2023-sch-6-sec-3 ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Attorney-General must provide consent to the transfer country." ;
    dc:description "Ministerial consent, information relevant to the transfer" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
